port 8080) on node2's transit-side address 10.10.12.2:80 via OPNsense port-forward, and gave node3 (on lan-a) a static route through node1 to reach that address. Verified node3 reaches the service only via node2's address, never node4 directly. All four nodes were then restarted one at a time per the mandatory protocol, each with confirmed changed boot identity and confirmed post-restart recovery of configuration, service, and connectivity.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Mapped physical topology via ARP/tcpdump probing: node1.eth1<->node2.vtnet1 (transit), node1.eth2<->node3.enp8s0 (lan-a), node2.vtnet2<->node4.enp8s0 (lan-b)\",\"Assigned static addressing: transit net 10.10.12.0/24 (node1=.1, node2=.2), lan-a net 10.10.13.0/24 (node1=.1, node3=.2), lan-b net 10.10.14.0/24 (node2=.1, node4=.2)\",\"Configured node1 (VyOS) eth1/eth2 addresses via configure/commit/save; confirmed ip_forward=1 and no firewall filter blocking forwarding\",\"Configured node2 (OPNsense) via config.xml edits: assigned opt1(vtnet1)/opt2(vtnet2) interfaces with static IPs, added a gateway object plus a static route to 10.10.13.0/24 via node1's transit address, added a port-forward (DNAT) rule on opt1 tcp/80 -> 10.10.14.2:8080, and a matching pass filter rule targeting the post-NAT destination (had to fix this since pf filter rules evaluate after NAT rewrite, so a rule matching the pre-NAT address never matched)\",\"Configured node3 and node4 networking persistently via systemd-networkd unit files (overriding the wildcard DHCP=yes match); added node3's route to 10.10.12.0/24 via node1, and node4's route to 10.10.13.0/24 via node2 (fixed an asymmetric-routing dead end where node4's replies were taking its management default route instead of returning via node2)\",\"Stood up a real HTTP service on node4:8080 via a systemd unit (demo-http.service) since none was running initially\",\"Verified end-to-end: node3 curl to http://10.10.12.2:80/ succeeds and returns node4's content; node3 to node4's address 10.10.14.2:8080 directly times out (no route/path), confirming node3 only reaches the service by asking node2\",\"Restarted node1, node2, node3, node4 one at a time (native reboot), polling each until exec was available again, confirming changed boot identity (boot_id or kern.boottime) and re-verifying config, service, and full two-hop connectivity after each restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline healthy state before any restarts (config, service, connectivity)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-98d03cbd91f143fd\",\"cmd-ec184af7615043dc\",\"cmd-6f2a8e64dab34f7c\",\"cmd-f0941e5d5f1c4c49\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot identity plus interface/route/service state on all 4 nodes, and a successful curl from node3 to the published service, immediately before starting the restart sequence.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Service published on node2's transit address (port 80) forwarding to node4:8080, and node3 reaching it via node2 rather than node4 directly\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c602f00a659b4329\",\"cmd-5c9ebecb565a45df\"],\"summary\":\"curl http://10.10.12.2:80/ from node3 returns node4's content across 3 repeated calls; direct curl to node4's address 10.10.14.2:8080 from node3 times out, proving the two-hop-only path.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 given a route enabling node3 to reach node2's transit address\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fcfb1e91236a43e7\",\"cmd-0d24a0c3e1c44dd1\",\"cmd-5a7f719e41984cfd\"],\"summary\":\"node1's eth1 (transit, 10.10.12.1/24) and eth2 (lan-a, 10.10.13.1/24) addresses configured and committed on VyOS, giving it directly-connected routes to both segments; node3 given a matching static route to 10.10.12.0/24 via node1.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgment, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-98d03cbd91f143fd\",\"cmd-6693c42174c14082\",\"cmd-850db62601534ff0\",\"cmd-2e7c973f9afa4f9d\",\"cmd-ed245ddd59b74611\",\"cmd-2e07e6486e8940b5\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 2674ee60...; reboot command acknowledged; immediate re-check still showed old boot_id (not yet restarted) then connection timed out during reboot; post-poll boot_id changed to 91c69730... with fresh uptime; interfaces/forwarding and service reachability confirmed recovered.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgment, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ec184af7615043dc\",\"cmd-51afdfa104c94f8c\",\"cmd-0b6a371d873d455d\",\"cmd-c95847b8398f4f38\",\"cmd-7c914c4337314958\",\"cmd-601ad9b98c974766\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline kern.boottime 14:59:15; reboot command issued (SSH session dropped, confirming restart in progress); post-poll kern.boottime changed to 15:13:22; interface IPs, NAT rule, and static route confirmed restored from config.xml, and service reachable end-to-end again.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgment, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6f2a8e64dab34f7c\",\"cmd-e50e0b831f894bdf\",\"cmd-75fd7f2721704daf\",\"cmd-461f306d767749b1\",\"cmd-c13d74b719f64d94\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 37344ae4...; reboot acknowledged then connection timed out; post-poll boot_id changed to b05cce6b... with fresh uptime; enp8s0 address and static route to transit net confirmed restored via systemd-networkd persisted unit, and service reachable again.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node4 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgment, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f0941e5d5f1c4c49\",\"cmd-474aaf7dcbe747cd\",\"cmd-bfa08a2eac9d4e25\",\"cmd-eaf000cd44244a24\",\"cmd-802be4991ec54e42\",\"cmd-4e0161e537ce4aaa\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id df9e2dce...; reboot acknowledged (connection reset confirming restart in progress); post-poll boot_id changed to f66d0af0... with fresh uptime; enp8s0 address, route to lan-a, and demo-http.service (enabled unit) confirmed restored/active; final end-to-end curl from node3 through node2 succeeded again post-restart.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Published node4's HTTP service (port 8080) on node2's transit-side address 10.10.12.2:80 via OPNsense port-forward, and gave node3 (on lan-a) a static route through node1 to reach that address. Verified node3 reaches the service only via node2's address, never node4 directly. All four nodes were then restarted one at a time per the mandatory protocol, each with confirmed changed boot identity and confirmed post-restart recovery of configuration, service, and connectivity.","actions_performed":["Mapped physical topology via ARP/tcpdump probing: node1.eth1<->node2.vtnet1 (transit), node1.eth2<->node3.enp8s0 (lan-a), node2.vtnet2<->node4.enp8s0 (lan-b)","Assigned static addressing: transit net 10.10.12.0/24 (node1=.1, node2=.2), lan-a net 10.10.13.0/24 (node1=.1, node3=.2), lan-b net 10.10.14.0/24 (node2=.1, node4=.2)","Configured node1 (VyOS) eth1/eth2 addresses via configure/commit/save; confirmed ip_forward=1 and no firewall filter blocking forwarding","Configured node2 (OPNsense) via config.xml edits: assigned opt1(vtnet1)/opt2(vtnet2) interfaces with static IPs, added a gateway object plus a static route to 10.10.13.0/24 via node1's transit address, added a port-forward (DNAT) rule on opt1 tcp/80 -> 10.10.14.2:8080, and a matching pass filter rule targeting the post-NAT destination (had to fix this since pf filter rules evaluate after NAT rewrite, so a rule matching the pre-NAT address never matched)","Configured node3 and node4 networking persistently via systemd-networkd unit files (overriding the wildcard DHCP=yes match); added node3's route to 10.10.12.0/24 via node1, and node4's route to 10.10.13.0/24 via node2 (fixed an asymmetric-routing dead end where node4's replies were taking its management default route instead of returning via node2)","Stood up a real HTTP service on node4:8080 via a systemd unit (demo-http.service) since none was running initially","Verified end-to-end: node3 curl to http://10.10.12.2:80/ succeeds and returns node4's content; node3 to node4's address 10.10.14.2:8080 directly times out (no route/path), confirming node3 only reaches the service by asking node2","Restarted node1, node2, node3, node4 one at a time (native reboot), polling each until exec was available again, confirming changed boot identity (boot_id or kern.boottime) and re-verifying config, service, and full two-hop connectivity after each restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline healthy state before any restarts (config, service, connectivity)","command_ids":["cmd-98d03cbd91f143fd","cmd-ec184af7615043dc","cmd-6f2a8e64dab34f7c","cmd-f0941e5d5f1c4c49"],"summary":"Captured boot identity plus interface/route/service state on all 4 nodes, and a successful curl from node3 to the published service, immediately before starting the restart sequence."},{"requirement":"Service published on node2's transit address (port 80) forwarding to node4:8080, and node3 reaching it via node2 rather than node4 directly","command_ids":["cmd-c602f00a659b4329","cmd-5c9ebecb565a45df"],"summary":"curl http://10.10.12.2:80/ from node3 returns node4's content across 3 repeated calls; direct curl to node4's address 10.10.14.2:8080 from node3 times out, proving the two-hop-only path."},{"requirement":"node1 given a route enabling node3 to reach node2's transit address","command_ids":["cmd-fcfb1e91236a43e7","cmd-0d24a0c3e1c44dd1","cmd-5a7f719e41984cfd"],"summary":"node1's eth1 (transit, 10.10.12.1/24) and eth2 (lan-a, 10.10.13.1/24) addresses configured and committed on VyOS, giving it directly-connected routes to both segments; node3 given a matching static route to 10.10.12.0/24 via node1."},{"requirement":"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgment, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-98d03cbd91f143fd","cmd-6693c42174c14082","cmd-850db62601534ff0","cmd-2e7c973f9afa4f9d","cmd-ed245ddd59b74611","cmd-2e07e6486e8940b5"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 2